Package: herald
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, bash (>= 4.0), systemd, curl, python3, coreutils
Suggests: update-motd
Description: print a quote at the top of every new terminal and at login
 herald is a small Linux daemon and CLI that prints a daily quote. It
 supports two display surfaces:
 .
   * Terminal greeting at the top of every new interactive shell, via
     /etc/profile.d/ plus a one-block opt-in in the user's ~/.bashrc.
   * Login MOTD via /etc/update-motd.d/, shown at SSH/console/display-
     manager login (requires the 'update-motd' package on Debian/Ubuntu).
 .
 Both are off by default; toggle with 'herald terminal' and 'herald motd'
 (or 'herald all'). Quotes are fetched from zenquotes.io with a 1.5s
 timeout, with a fallback to a bundled local pool of about 30 curated
 quotes. The cache is refreshed by a systemd timer every three hours by
 default; configurable via 'herald set-refresh <hours>'.
 .
 An optional /etc/herald.prefix file lets you prepend custom text above
 the quote (useful for hostname banners, contact info, etc.).
 .
 DISCLAIMER: provided AS IS, no warranty. Quotes are fetched from a
 third-party service. The author is not liable for the content of fetched
 quotes, for events outside the author's control (third-party API outage,
 downstream modifications, supply-chain compromise), or for any damage
 caused by installing or running this software. See README for full text.
